{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "8294724",
      "title": "Handling Form Submission & Validation",
      "sourceHash": "e7a71781832b8af33eab1f0a9d91fefbf0d76f826c12ed5b70a9774550ec8c35",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.72,
          "end": 3.6,
          "en": "So now that we have this checkout form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.6,
          "end": 5.04,
          "en": "in place here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.04,
          "end": 8.13,
          "en": "it's time to also deal with the actual form submission",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.13,
          "end": 11.01,
          "en": "so that thereafter we can send that request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.01,
          "end": 14.97,
          "en": "to the backend and submit the order to the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.97,
          "end": 19.35,
          "en": "And of course, here we already have a form element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.35,
          "end": 22.47,
          "en": "so if we wanna handle the submission of this form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.47,
          "end": 26.97,
          "en": "we can either do that manually by adding the onSubmit prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.97,
          "end": 29.85,
          "en": "and setting up our own function that's triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.85,
          "end": 31.92,
          "en": "when that submit event occurs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.92,
          "end": 35.16,
          "en": "or we could use a form action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.16,
          "end": 39,
          "en": "Now, here, I'll start by using this onSubmit prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39,
          "end": 42.39,
          "en": "and I'll handle the form submission manually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.39,
          "end": 45.63,
          "en": "I'll not use this form actions feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.63,
          "end": 47.85,
          "en": "that's offered by React, but later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.85,
          "end": 49.59,
          "en": "at the end of this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.59,
          "end": 54.59,
          "en": "we'll actually migrate this project to use form actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.63,
          "end": 58.17,
          "en": "so that you see both approaches in action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.17,
          "end": 61.86,
          "en": "So therefore here, I'll start by adding this onSubmit prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.86,
          "end": 63.84,
          "en": "to this form element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.84,
          "end": 66.128,
          "en": "And then we can set up a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.128,
          "end": 68.16,
          "en": "handleSubmit could be the name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.16,
          "end": 70.02,
          "en": "which we connect to that prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.02,
          "end": 73.743,
          "en": "so which we pass as a value to that prop as we always do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.18,
          "end": 78.48,
          "en": "Now, as you learned in the forms course section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.48,
          "end": 80.73,
          "en": "the thing with forum submissions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.73,
          "end": 83.34,
          "en": "just is that out of the box,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.34,
          "end": 87.66,
          "en": "when using a regular button in a regular form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.66,
          "end": 91.74,
          "en": "the browser will go ahead and create an HTTTP request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.74,
          "end": 94.47,
          "en": "for you and send it for you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.47,
          "end": 97.25999999999999,
          "en": "but unfortunately not to the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.25999999999999,
          "end": 99.3,
          "en": "we want it to be sent to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.3,
          "end": 101.52000000000001,
          "en": "because the browser doesn't know about that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.52000000000001,
          "end": 103.2,
          "en": "It's a standalone process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.2,
          "end": 106.143,
          "en": "and it would be a standalone server on the internet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.34,
          "end": 110.4,
          "en": "Instead, the browser would send the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.4,
          "end": 113.78999999999999,
          "en": "to this development server that's serving this site.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.78999999999999,
          "end": 115.71000000000001,
          "en": "So our front end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.71000000000001,
          "end": 119.85,
          "en": "But this server and this site is not prepared",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.85,
          "end": 122.43299999999999,
          "en": "and equipped to handle this request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 123.63,
          "end": 125.22,
          "en": "Therefore, what we need to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.22,
          "end": 128.07,
          "en": "is we need to prevent that default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 128.07,
          "end": 129.78,
          "en": "And as you learned, we can do this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 129.78,
          "end": 134.64,
          "en": "by calling preventDefault on that standard event object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.64,
          "end": 136.92000000000002,
          "en": "which we automatically receive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 136.92000000000002,
          "end": 139.77,
          "en": "in our event handling function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139.77,
          "end": 142.89,
          "en": "It's passed in by React in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 142.89,
          "end": 146.52,
          "en": "And by calling this method here, preventDefault,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 146.52,
          "end": 148.86,
          "en": "we make sure that this request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 148.86,
          "end": 151.07999999999998,
          "en": "which otherwise would get created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 151.07999999999998,
          "end": 154.233,
          "en": "and sent is not getting created and sent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.43,
          "end": 158.49,
          "en": "Therefore now we have a chance to control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.49,
          "end": 161.253,
          "en": "what should happen when that form is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 162.21,
          "end": 164.64,
          "en": "And what should happen here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 164.64,
          "end": 169.64,
          "en": "is that A, the input values should get validated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.16,
          "end": 174.063,
          "en": "so that an empty form, for example, can't be submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 175.17000000000002,
          "end": 177,
          "en": "And B, I wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 177,
          "end": 179.703,
          "en": "that I get hold of the entered values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 180.75,
          "end": 183.24,
          "en": "Now here to validate the input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 183.24,
          "end": 187.89,
          "en": "I added the required prop on those input fields.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 187.89,
          "end": 190.14,
          "en": "And as a result, if we save that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 190.14,
          "end": 191.91,
          "en": "and we go to the Checkout page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 191.91,
          "end": 194.43,
          "en": "and we try to submit an empty form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 194.43,
          "end": 197.64,
          "en": "we get some nice error messages here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 197.64,
          "end": 198.75,
          "en": "So that's pretty good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 198.75,
          "end": 201.6,
          "en": "We don't have to worry about this problem here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 201.6,
          "end": 203.43,
          "en": "Though, as mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 203.43,
          "end": 207.75,
          "en": "you could of course also implement custom Java script-driven",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 207.75,
          "end": 212.13,
          "en": "validation as you also learned it in the forms section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 212.13,
          "end": 213.93,
          "en": "But here, I'll keep it like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 213.93,
          "end": 216.993,
          "en": "and therefore the validation part is already done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 218.28,
          "end": 221.01,
          "en": "Now, when it comes to extracting the values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 221.01,
          "end": 223.32,
          "en": "we also got multiple options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 223.32,
          "end": 227.49,
          "en": "We could add a state value for every input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 227.49,
          "end": 231.48,
          "en": "or a combined state object for all the inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 231.48,
          "end": 233.424,
          "en": "and use the onChange prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 233.424,
          "end": 236.94,
          "en": "to update the state on every keystroke.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 236.94,
          "end": 238.17000000000002,
          "en": "We could do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 238.17000000000002,
          "end": 240.63,
          "en": "and for some validation approaches",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 240.63,
          "end": 243.39,
          "en": "where we wanna validate on every keystroke,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 243.39,
          "end": 245.763,
          "en": "we typically would have to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 246.75,
          "end": 250.26,
          "en": "Alternatively, we could work with refs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 250.26,
          "end": 252.81,
          "en": "Now, since I have a custom component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 252.81,
          "end": 256.44,
          "en": "the input component, in order to pass a ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 256.44,
          "end": 260.43,
          "en": "to that component, you might need to use forward ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 260.43,
          "end": 264.03,
          "en": "and wrap that component function with forward ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 264.03,
          "end": 268.02,
          "en": "if you're using a React version lower than 19.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 268.02,
          "end": 271.38,
          "en": "If you are using React version 19 or higher,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 271.38,
          "end": 274.44,
          "en": "you could simply pass a ref to this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 274.44,
          "end": 276.12,
          "en": "and use it in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 276.12,
          "end": 277.29,
          "en": "But here again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 277.29,
          "end": 281.1,
          "en": "I instead prefer using the built-in features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 281.1,
          "end": 283.65,
          "en": "the browser offers to us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 283.65,
          "end": 287.01,
          "en": "We can create such a FormData object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 287.01,
          "end": 289.2,
          "en": "and pass the event target,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 289.2,
          "end": 291.63,
          "en": "which is the form element in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 291.63,
          "end": 294.65999999999997,
          "en": "the underlying object that's managed by the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 294.65999999999997,
          "end": 296.22,
          "en": "to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 296.22,
          "end": 300.6,
          "en": "Pass that to the FormData constructor function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 300.6,
          "end": 304.17,
          "en": "And what we'll get back is an object that makes it very easy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 304.17,
          "end": 307.533,
          "en": "for us to get hold of those user entered values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 308.49,
          "end": 310.65,
          "en": "The the only important thing here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 310.65,
          "end": 314.55,
          "en": "is that we got this name prop on our inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 314.55,
          "end": 316.65,
          "en": "because this is required",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 316.65,
          "end": 320.505,
          "en": "to then access those different input fields",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 320.505,
          "end": 324.903,
          "en": "by their name and to extract the values entered by the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 326.55,
          "end": 328.92,
          "en": "Because as you learned, we can now use the get method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 328.92,
          "end": 332.15999999999997,
          "en": "for example, to get the full name value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 332.15999999999997,
          "end": 334.563,
          "en": "So the value that was entered into this field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 335.76,
          "end": 339.15,
          "en": "Or as you also learned in the forms section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 339.15,
          "end": 343.26,
          "en": "we can actually convert this FormData object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 343.26,
          "end": 346.02,
          "en": "to a simpler JavaScript object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 346.02,
          "end": 350.01,
          "en": "where those form inputs are basically represented",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 350.01,
          "end": 352.26,
          "en": "by their name as property names,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 352.26,
          "end": 356.46,
          "en": "and the entered values are then values for those properties,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 356.46,
          "end": 359.73,
          "en": "by using object fromEntries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 359.73,
          "end": 363.273,
          "en": "and passing FormData entries like this to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 364.17,
          "end": 367.11,
          "en": "And this will essentially give us an object where we,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 367.11,
          "end": 370.86,
          "en": "for example, have an email property with the value entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 370.86,
          "end": 371.793,
          "en": "by the user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 372.96,
          "end": 374.88,
          "en": "and of course key value pairs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 374.88,
          "end": 377.103,
          "en": "for all the other input fields as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 378.15,
          "end": 382.23,
          "en": "And therefore, this is how we can easily extract the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 382.23,
          "end": 383.97,
          "en": "entered by the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 383.97,
          "end": 387.6,
          "en": "And that's then the data which we in the end wanna send",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 387.6,
          "end": 390.99,
          "en": "to the backend, combined with the cart data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 390.99,
          "end": 392.82,
          "en": "because of course the order",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 392.82,
          "end": 395.94,
          "en": "which we're sending to the backend should also include",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 395.94,
          "end": 398.463,
          "en": "details about what was ordered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 399.48,
          "end": 402.6,
          "en": "And therefore that's now the last step here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 402.6,
          "end": 407.04,
          "en": "We need to send such an HTTP request to the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 407.04,
          "end": 408.663,
          "en": "So let's do that as a next step.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}